/* book exam traps: The fuel-air cycle is still ideal: it has no friction, no heat loss and no pumping. Those belong to the actual cycle. | Variable specific heat lowers the peak temperature for the same heat input; it does not raise it. The specific heat goes up, so ΔT = q/cv goes down. | Maximum power and maximum efficiency do not come at the same mixture: power slightly rich, efficiency lean. | The pumping loop is subtracted from the main loop to get net indicated work, not added. | Indicated efficiency is before friction; brake efficiency is ηi × ηm. Percentage points are not per cent: 56.5 % to 32.3 % is a fall of 24.2 points, or 43 per cent of the ideal value. */
